### { "data": {
###     "answer": "TOE HOLD" },
###   "difficulty": 3,
###   "estimatedSeconds": 240,
###   "id": "2026-08-20:phrazle:abcd1234",
###   "type": "phrazle" }
###
### Wordle for phrases: guess the phrase, every guess a real word of the right length, four tile
### states instead of three. UNLIMITED ATTEMPTS -- see below.
###
### `answer` IS NOT A SECRET, and it is documented as one rather than obscured. The board paints its
### characters as tiles and marks them LOCALLY, so marking needs the letters: a hash cannot color a
### tile, and an encoding would ship its own reversal in the same bundle -- a CLAIM of secrecy, which
### is more dangerous than an admitted absence of one because the next person builds a control on top
### of it. The pack sits in localStorage where three keystrokes reveal it anyway. This API does not
### attempt anti-cheat and is not designed for it.
###
### It is the CANONICAL FORM -- uppercase A-Z words separated by single spaces -- and it is the only
### phrase-type answer that is not the corpus text verbatim, because the characters on the board must
### be the characters the marker marks. SPLIT IT TO GET THE GRID: the word lengths are
### `answer.split(' ').map((word) => word.length)`. There is no `wordLengths` field and there will not
### be -- two fields that can disagree is a board with the wrong number of tiles.
###
### THERE IS NO GUESS LIMIT AND NO LOSS STATE. This type shipped a `maxGuesses` of six until
### 2026-08-24. THE FIELD IS GONE -- not zero, not null, not present-and-ignored -- because a limit
### field claiming to have no limit is worse than no field: the next reader builds a bound on top of
### it. A player guesses until the phrase falls, and a board that runs out of rows grows another.
### Do not hard-code a limit, and do not reintroduce one client-side.
###
### KEEPING A BOUNDED WINDOW OF GUESSES IS STORAGE, NOT RULES, and it is yours to decide. Progress
### lives in localStorage, which is a text box a player can type into, so a client that reads it needs
### SOME ceiling on what it will render -- but that ceiling bounds a corrupt write, not a game, and
### nothing on the wire declares it.
###
### `category` IS PRESENT ON THIS TYPE'S BAND 2 AND ABSENT ON ITS BANDS 3 AND 5. Read the key; do not
### assume either way.
###
### THIS PARAGRAPH USED TO SAY THE OPPOSITE -- "absent on every phrazle puzzle, always" -- and it was
### falsified by a band change rather than by anything about categories. This type declared [3, 5]
### when that was written, and the visibility table hides the category at exactly 3 and 5, so the
### claim was true by coincidence of the two lists agreeing. It now declares [2, 3, 5], the table is
### unchanged, and band 2 therefore carries a category. A client told not to reserve space for it
### drops a label on a third of this type's puzzles.
###
### NO `hints` KEY, AND NO `phrazle-reveal` METADATA. Both were removed on 2026-08-31 and both are
### absent rather than empty. The `kind` union no longer has a member for this type.
###
### WHAT REPLACED THEM. The old ladder walked positions -- "Letter 1 of word 1 is T." -- choosing them
### the night before, so it could not see that four guesses had already established that tile. The
### device now computes rungs about the LETTER ECONOMY of the phrase, against what the player's own
### guesses have ruled in and out: common letters the phrase does NOT contain, then uncommon letters it
### DOES, then one word's letters out of order. `answer` is all it needs and `answer` already ships.
###
### THIS IS THE SECOND RULE THIS TYPE COMPUTES LOCALLY RATHER THAN RECEIVING, and for the same reason
### as the first. Marking is the client's because a per-guess endpoint would be a round trip in an
### offline-first design and an unauthenticated oracle besides; hints are the client's because a rung
### that cannot see the board cannot know what is still worth saying. Both run over something the
### player invents at play time. That criterion ADMITS a rule to `src/rules/`; it does not put one
### there. `src/rules/` is for rules BOTH repos run, and nothing in this repo ever called the hint
### builder -- so marking is vendored in both and the rung builder lives only in lull-ui.
###
### MARKING IS THE CLIENT'S, AND IT IS THE ONE RULE THIS API DOES NOT SHIP AS DATA. There is no
### per-guess endpoint and there will not be one: it would need a round trip per guess in an
### offline-first design, and nothing here authenticates a player, so a marking endpoint would be an
### unauthenticated oracle anyone could walk to recover the answer faster than reading it off the
### wire. The rules are vendored as source (`src/rules/mark-guess.ts`, `src/rules/is-valid-guess.ts`)
### and hand-copied into the client. THE FOUR TILE STATES ARE ASSIGNMENT OUTCOMES, NOT MEMBERSHIP
### TESTS, and the difference is where every implementation of this goes wrong:
###
###   green   right letter, right position, right word
###   yellow  an UNSPENT copy of this letter remains in this word, at another position
###   purple  an UNSPENT copy remains elsewhere in the phrase, and none in this word
###   gray    no unspent copy remains anywhere in the phrase
###
### ONE PHRASE-WIDE LEDGER, debited by greens, then yellows, then purples. The passes run GLOBALLY BY
### COLOR -- every green, then every yellow, then every purple -- and strictly left to right within
### each pass. Running all three passes for word 1 before starting word 2 is WRONG: purple reads the
### phrase-wide sum, so it can spend a copy a later word's green is entitled to. For every letter,
### `green + yellow + purple <= occurrences in the answer`. A board showing a letter more colored
### tiles than the phrase contains is a lie the player can prove by counting.
###
### A GUESS IS CORRECT IFF EVERY TILE IS GREEN. There is no separate comparison rule for this type,
### and adding one would create two definitions of "correct" that can disagree.
###
### A GUESS THAT FAILS VALIDATION DOES NOT COST AN ATTEMPT. Reject it at the keyboard: right number
### of words, right length per word, A-Z only, and every word in the guess dictionary from
### GET /dictionary/{version}, documented near the top of this file.
###
### THE BOARD IS NOW UP TO SIX ROWS OF UP TO ELEVEN TILES, where it was three of seven. `answer` is
### two to six words, each two to eleven letters, thirty letters or fewer in total -- so a renderer
### that assumed at most three rows, at most seven tiles, or a three-letter minimum per row is wrong
### on phrases this API already emits. TWO-LETTER WORDS ARE ORDINARY here: OUT OF THE BLUE and PIECE
### OF THE ACTION are typical answers, not edge cases. Single-letter words remain impossible.
###
### PROGRESS: { "guesses": string[] } -- in order, in the same canonical form `answer` uses, and
### VALID GUESSES ONLY. MARKS ARE DERIVED ON EVERY RENDER AND NEVER STORED, so a corrected marking
### rule recolors old boards instead of contradicting them. `solved` is derivable: true iff some
### guess marks all green. THERE IS NO LOSS: the only two states are solved and still going.
### Prune progress WITH its pack, in the same pass -- a resumed board whose pack is gone has no
### `answer` to mark against, which is the one combination that cannot be rendered at all.
###
### --- end phrazle ---
